@node What is SotF
@section What is SotF

SotF (@emph{Sound of the Future}, after the Giorgio Moroder song) is a
free, open-source desktop audio stack written almost entirely in Rust.
A single workspace contains:

@itemize @bullet
@item
A native audio player with a TUI front-end (terminal) and a desktop
front-end built on GPUI.
@item
An offline @strong{AutoEQ} optimiser that turns measurement data into
parametric EQ filters for speakers and headphones.
@item
An offline @strong{RoomEQ} optimiser that designs per-channel EQ,
delays and crossovers from in-room measurements.
@item
A plugin @strong{host} (mini DAW) that runs SotF plugins in a rack or
a graph, plus CLAP / VST3 / AU bridges.
@item
A library of audio plugins (EQ, dynamics, spatial, denoising, analysis,
A/B testing, @dots{}).
@item
On macOS, a system-wide HAL driver and menubar daemon so the plugin
chain can be applied to any application's output.
@end itemize

@node Feature Highlights
@section Feature Highlights

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Optimisation:} differential evolution (forked from SciPy)
with JADE/adaptive variants, plus bridges to NLopt and metaheuristics.
@item
@strong{Filters:} IIR/FIR with parametric EQ, linear-phase EQ,
linear-phase crossovers, warped/Kautz topologies.
@item
@strong{Spatial audio:} 2.0 to 9.1.6 upmixing, binaural rendering,
cross-talk cancellation, ambisonics, beamforming.
@item
@strong{Analysis:} CEA2034 / Spinorama metrics, room impulse-response
analysis, spectrum and loudness meters.
@item
@strong{Portability:} pure Rust where possible, BLAS via Accelerate
(macOS), OpenBLAS (Linux, Windows ARM) or MKL (Windows x64).
@end itemize

@node Audience
@section Audience

This manual targets three overlapping audiences:

@table @asis
@item Listeners
People who want their headphones, speakers or room to sound right.
Read @ref{User Guide} and the @ref{Concepts} chapter.
@item Power users / measurers
People who already have REW or Klippel data and want to design their
own filters. Read @ref{User Guide}, @ref{CLI Reference} and the
@ref{Plugins Reference}.
@item Developers
Contributors and integrators. Read @ref{Developer Guide},
@ref{Workspace and Crates} and @ref{API Reference}.
@end table

@node Project Philosophy
@section Project Philosophy

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Rust first.} C/C++ dependencies are minimised so the stack
stays portable and auditable.
@item
@strong{Business logic in libraries.} The @code{sotf-player} crate
owns playback logic; @code{app-tui} and @code{app-gpui} are thin
front-ends. No duplication.
@item
@strong{Real-time correctness.} Audio callbacks must never allocate or
lock. Pre-allocate in @code{build()}, reuse via @code{Option::take()}
in @code{process()}.
@item
@strong{Measurement-driven.} Filters and metrics are validated against
published data (Spinorama, CEA2034, Equalizer APO output).
@end itemize

