@node autoeq CLI
@section @code{autoeq}

Offline AutoEQ optimiser. Given an anechoic speaker measurement or
a headphone measurement plus a target curve, produces parametric
filters. Output formats include JSON, Equalizer APO, REW, and SotF
plugin presets.

@example
autoeq --speaker "Genelec 8341A" --target harman --filters 10 \
       --output out.txt --format apo
@end example

@node roomeq CLI
@section @code{roomeq}

Multichannel in-room optimiser. Input is a measurement bundle (per-
channel impulse responses or sweeps); output is a per-channel filter
+ delay + crossover description that can be loaded as a SotF plugin
graph.

See @file{crates/autoeq/bin/roomeq/INPUT_FORMAT.md} and
@file{OUTPUT_FORMAT.md} for the file formats.

@node convert-recording CLI
@section @code{convert-recording}

