@node Building from Source
@section Building from Source

Install Rust via @uref{https://rustup.rs}, then:

@example
cargo install just
just                       # list targets
just install-macos         # or just install-linux-* / windows
just post-install
just download-once         # speaker / SOFA data
just build
just test
@end example

Front-ends:

@example
cargo build -p app-cli --release       # CLI player
just tui                               # TUI player
just gpui                              # desktop GPUI player
@end example

Signed macOS builds:

@example
./scripts/build-systemwide.sh
./scripts/build-dmg-sotf.sh
@end example

@node Workflow and Tooling
@section Workflow and Tooling

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{cargo check --workspace} and @code{cargo clippy
  --workspace} after every change.
@item @code{cargo test --workspace} (or @code{-p <crate>}) before
  reporting a task done. Compilation is not proof of correctness.
@item Plugins and engine crates: build with
  @code{--no-default-features} when @code{hdf5-metno-sys} is in the
  dep tree.
@item Python tooling: use @file{./venv/bin/python} and
  @file{./venv/bin/pyright}. Never the system Python.
@item @code{just qa} runs the optimiser benchmark suite.
@end itemize

@node Coding Rules
@section Coding Rules

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Never use @code{unsafe} without asking.}
@item Business logic goes in @code{sotf-player} (or in the relevant
  @code{math-*} / @code{autoeq} crate). App crates are thin UI
  wrappers.
@item Before editing a file, verify it is actively compiled (not
  behind a disabled feature, not orphaned).
@item @code{cargo check} after edits. The editor reporting success
  means bytes hit disk, not that code compiles.
@item Crash hard on unknown enum values. Do not add a default arm
  that silently absorbs them.
@end itemize

Naming:

@table @asis
@item User-facing binaries
@code{kebab-case} (@code{sotf-desktop}, @code{sotf-tui},
@code{sotf-systemwide}).
@item Internal CLI tools
@code{snake_case} (@code{autoeq_download_speakers}).
@item Dist artefacts
@code{name-version-os-arch.format}, lowercase. Debian @code{.deb}
keeps its @code{_}-separated convention.
@item Crates
@code{kebab-case}.
@item Module files
@code{snake_case}.
@end table

@node Real-time Discipline
@section Real-time Discipline

Audio is real-time soft. A late frame is a click. Rules:

@itemize @bullet
@item No allocation in @code{process()}.
@item No locking in @code{process()}. Cache per-frame predicates in
  @code{build()}.
@item No @code{println!}, no @code{log::*} from the audio thread.
  Use lock-free SPSC channels to signal the UI.
@item Output saturation must be clamped in the cpal callback, not
  inside plugins.
@end itemize

@node Adding a Plugin
@section Adding a Plugin

@enumerate
@item Create @file{crates/sotf-plugins/crates/sotf-plugin-foo/}.
@item Add the crate to the workspace @file{Cargo.toml}.
@item Implement the @code{Plugin} trait (see
  @ref{Plugin trait}).
@item Define a @code{PARAMS: &[ParamSpec]} array (see
  @ref{Plugin Parameter Registration}).
@item Register the plugin in the host's factory.
@item Add a unit test (golden buffer or property test).
@item Run @code{cargo run -p sotf-docs-gen} to regenerate the
  reference page.
@end enumerate

@node Plugin Parameter Registration
@section Plugin Parameter Registration

@cindex parameter registration
A plugin parameter must be wired in @strong{three} places, or it is
silently ignored:

@enumerate
@item @code{rebuild_cached_parameters}: insert the parameter into
  @code{cached_parameters}.
@item @code{set_parameter}: handle inbound updates.
@item @code{get_parameter}: report current value.
@end enumerate

Missing the @code{cached_parameters} step causes silent rejection of
updates -- the most common foot-gun when adding parameters.

@node Testing and QA
@section Testing and QA

@itemize @bullet
@item Unit tests live next to the code they cover.
@item Integration tests live in @file{tests/} of each crate.
@item @code{just qa} runs the optimisation benchmark suite
  (long-running).
@item Audio bugs (crackling, saturation, pitch shift) need
  signal-chain tracing, not surface patches.
@end itemize

@node Code Review
@section Code Review

@itemize @bullet
@item Every change to @code{sotf-engine} or @code{sotf-plugins} is
  its own PR and must go through the @code{pr-review-toolkit:code-reviewer}.
@item Other crates: use @code{/code-review}.
@item Reviews must include: correctness bugs with test cases, edge
  cases in algorithm logic, missing error handling, and concrete
  fixes. Surface reviews are rejected.
@end itemize

