@node sotf-engine API
@section @code{sotf-engine} API

Key types:

@table @code
@item Engine
The owner of the four-thread pipeline. Construct with
@code{Engine::new(config)}, drive with @code{start()} / @code{stop()}.
@item NodeBuffer
Lock-free, single-writer/single-reader buffer used between processing
nodes. Replaces the older @code{AudioBuffer = Arc<Mutex<Vec<f32>>>}.
@item AudioFrame
Owned @code{Vec<f32>} of interleaved samples for a single processing
quantum. Allocated once, sent across the channel.
@item DawHost
Wraps an @code{Arc<Mutex<Box<dyn Plugin>>>} per node so plugins can
optionally be touched cross-thread.
@end table

@noindent
Real-time invariants:

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{process()} takes @code{&mut self} (processing is single-
  threaded).
@item Buffers are split out into a @code{ProcessBuffers} struct so
  the borrow checker accepts the mutable-buffer / immutable-graph
  pattern; put-back is done with @code{Option::take()}.
@end itemize

@node sotf-player API
@section @code{sotf-player} API

Controllers (in @file{controllers/}):

@table @code
@item LibraryController
Filtering, sorting, pagination, navigation, directory management.
@item QueueController
Wraps @code{Queue}; mutations return a @code{QueuePlaybackEffect}.
Implements @code{Deref}, @code{DerefMut}, @code{IntoIterator}.
@item PlaybackController
Volume, mute, replay gain, play tracking.
@item ScanController
Wraps the ReplayGain, Waveform and Bliss managers
(@code{update_all}, @code{stop_all}).
@item PluginController
(In progress.) Plugin chain manipulation.
@end table

App-side state types (@code{app/state/} in each app crate) are
thin wrappers around these controllers via @code{Deref}.

@node Plugin trait
@section The @code{Plugin} trait
@cindex Plugin trait

Every DSP plugin implements a trait roughly shaped as:

@example
pub trait Plugin: Send @{
    fn build(&mut self, ctx: &BuildContext) -> Result<()>;
    fn process(&mut self, ctx: &mut ProcessContext) -> Result<usize>;
    fn set_parameter(&mut self, id: ParamId, value: ParamValue);
    fn get_parameter(&self, id: ParamId) -> ParamValue;
    fn params(&self) -> &'static [ParamSpec];
    fn rebuild_cached_parameters(&mut self);
@}
@end example

@noindent
Notes:

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{process()} must return @code{context.num_frames} for
  STFT-style plugins to keep the ring buffer aligned.
@item Per-frame checks must be cached in @code{build()}; locking a
  plugin mutex per frame causes audible jitter.
@item Plugin parameter changes must reach
  @code{rebuild_cached_parameters()}, @code{set_parameter()} and
  @code{get_parameter()} or they are silently dropped.
@end itemize

@node Plugin Config and ParamSpec
@section @code{PluginConfig} and @code{ParamSpec}

@code{PluginConfig} is the JSON-friendly description used to
instantiate plugins from configs, sessions and the CLI:

@example
pub struct PluginConfig @{
    pub plugin_type: String,
    pub parameters: serde_json::Value,
@}
@end example

@code{ParamSpec} is the static description used by the docs
generator, the UI editor and the host's param indexer:

@example
pub struct ParamSpec @{
    pub name: &'static str,
    pub kind: ParamType,        // Float, Int, Bool, Choice, FilePath
    pub update_mode: UpdateMode,// rt, rebuild
    pub display_scale: f32,     // 1.0, 100.0 (%) , 1000.0 (x1000)
    pub default: ParamValue,
    pub range: ParamRange,
    pub unit: &'static str,
    pub group: &'static str,
    pub description: &'static str,
@}
@end example

