@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting

@cindex troubleshooting
@cindex crackling
@cindex saturation

@table @asis
@item Audio crackles on macOS, debug builds
Aggressive debug optimisation breaks cpal/CoreAudio device
enumeration. Keep @code{opt-level = 0} for debug.
@item Audio crackles in any build
You almost certainly allocated or locked in the audio path. Pre-
allocate in @code{build()} and use @code{Option::take()} in
@code{process()}. Cache per-frame predicates.
@item Plugin parameter changes have no effect
Check that the parameter is registered in all three places
(@code{rebuild_cached_parameters}, @code{set_parameter},
@code{get_parameter}). Most common cause: missing
@code{cached_parameters} entry.
@item @code{hdf5-metno-sys} fails to build
Build with @code{--no-default-features} on @code{sotf-plugins} or
@code{sotf-engine}.
@item @code{clap} CLI complains about duplicate fields
Look for duplicate field names across flattened structs (e.g.@: a
shared @code{enabled} between two sub-args).
@item Output is saturated or clipped
The clamp lives in the cpal callback. Don't clip inside plugins.
Check pre-gain and the limiter's ceiling.
@item Filters from RoomEQ are placed outside the measurement band
Verify the optimiser frequency range matches the measurement bounds.
Passband detection uses @emph{relative-to-peak} thresholds.
@item Bug reports without logs
Always capture the raw log first; do not guess from a symptom.
@end table

