@node FAQ
@chapter FAQ

@table @asis
@item Why is so much of this re-implemented in Rust?
The project is partly a learning vehicle and partly a portability
play: pure Rust avoids C/C++ build pain across macOS, Linux and
Windows and lets the optimiser run in WASM in the browser.

@item Could I use Camilla DSP instead of @code{sotf-engine}?
Yes -- early versions did. The engine was rewritten so plugin
authoring, profiling and UI integration could live in one tree.

@item Why GPUI and not Tauri / egui / Qt?
GPUI keeps the entire stack in Rust without a TypeScript context
switch, and gives enough control to wire audio meters to the
renderer cheaply.

@item Are AU plugins supported?
CLAP and VST3 work. AU works with a Swift wrapper around the FFI
crate. Native AU UIs from GPUI are still experimental.

@item Why is the macOS system-wide daemon not the default?
Loading a HAL driver and a daemon to capture system audio is
intrusive on macOS. It is opt-in and lives in @file{systemwide/}
plus @code{sotf-macos-configbar}.

@item How do I make my own listening profile?
Build a plugin chain that sounds right, then @samp{Save as profile}
from the desktop player. Profiles are JSON; you can edit them by
hand.
@end table

